<article class="env-lemma" id="05WW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05WW">Lemma <span data-tag="05WW">76.22.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X' \ar[r]_{g'} \ar[d]_{f'} &  X \ar[d]^ f \\  Y' \ar[r]^ g &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a cartesian diagram of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Assume $g$ is flat, $f$ is locally of finite presentation, and $\mathcal{F}$ is locally of finite presentation. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \{ x' \in |X'| : (g')^*\mathcal{F}\text{ is flat over }Y'\text{ at }x'\}   \]
</div>
  <p> is the inverse image of the open subset of Theorem <a href="/tag/05WV" data-tag="05WV">76.22.1</a> under the continuous map $|g'| : |X'| \to |X|$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/05VW" data-tag="05VW">67.31.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>